    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1655-a1">

                <pb facs="1195" n="1079" xml:id="pg1079"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ministry of Foreign Affairs to the American
                        Embassy</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sublime Porte</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 29, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In reply to the note verbale which the Embassy of the United States of America
                    was pleased to address to it under date of April 21 last, No. 268, the Ministry
                    of Foreign Affairs has the honor to inform it that it has just asked the German
                    Government to take under its protection Ottoman subjects and interests in the
                    city of Mexico, until the Government of the Republic shall there have a
                    representative.</p>
                <p>The Imperial Ministry therefore asks the Embassy of the Republic to kindly have
                    given, if that has not already been done, instructions to the American consuls
                    in the other cities of Mexico to undertake the protection of Ottoman subjects
                    living in their districts.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
